<%#
  Signs SLSA build provenance for an artifact via GitHub's official
  actions/attest-build-provenance (Sigstore → Rekor), verifiable with
  `gh attestation verify`. Used where the registry mints no native provenance (Ruby,
  and every custom build — ship-package verifies it); npm (--provenance) and PyPI
  (PEP 740) cover the turnkey js/py case. Requires id-token: write + attestations:
  write. The caller stamps the `if:` (not a dry run) and points subject_path at the
  artifact(s), attested BEFORE publish.

  @param subject_path [String, Array<String>] path/glob(s) to attest. Pass an array for
    multiple globs (e.g. ['dist/*.whl', 'dist/*.tar.gz']).
-%>
- name: Attest build provenance
  uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@0f67c3f4856b2e3261c31976d6725780e5e4c373 # v4.1.1
  with:
    subject-path: |-
<%- Array(locals.fetch(:subject_path)).each do |path| -%>
      <%= path %>
<%- end -%>
